.TH D_TUFT 1 "May 2026" "d_tuft 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
d_tuft \- Bidirectional EVM bytecode ↔ opcode transformer, analysis toolkit, and decompiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B d_tuft
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
d_tuft is a comprehensive EVM bytecode toolkit providing disassembly, assembly, comparison, function identification, gas analysis, stack simulation, execution, and full decompilation of Ethereum smart contract bytecode.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B disasm, d
Disassemble bytecode to readable opcodes.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft disasm <input> [options]
.IP
\fBOptions:\fR
.RS
.TP
.B -o, --output <file>
Write output to file (default: stdout)
.TP
.B -f, --format <format>
Output format: text (default), annotated, json
.TP
.B --no-pc
Omit program counter from output
.TP
.B --gas
Include gas cost per instruction
.TP
.B --hex
Include raw hex bytes per instruction
.TP
.B --stack
Run stack depth validation after disassembly
.RE
.TP
.B asm, a
Assemble opcodes to bytecode.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft asm <input.evm> [-o output.bin]
.TP
.B compare, c
Compare two bytecode or assembly files for equivalence.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft compare <file1> <file2> [--format auto|bytecode|assembly]
.TP
.B diff
Compare two contracts at function level to detect changes.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft diff <first> <second> [--format text|annotated|json]
.TP
.B identify, id
Identify public functions, resolve names from ABI, inspect contract structure.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft identify <input> [options]
.IP
\fBOptions:\fR
.RS
.TP
.B --format <format>
Output format: text (default), annotated, json
.TP
.B --abi <file>
ABI JSON file for function name resolution
.TP
.B -d, --diff <second_input>
Compare functions between two inputs
.TP
.B -o, --output [dir]
Save each function to its own file
.TP
.B --internal
List internal/private JUMPDESTs
.TP
.B --gas
Show gas cost estimates per function
.RE
.TP
.B gas, g
Analyse gas costs with per-opcode and per-category breakdowns.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft gas <input> [options]
.IP
\fBOptions:\fR
.RS
.TP
.B --functions
Break down gas per identified function
.TP
.B --top <n>
Number of hotspots to show (default: 5)
.TP
.B --window <n>
Hotspot sliding window size (default: 10)
.RE
.TP
.B stack, s
Simulate EVM stack execution, visualise depth, detect underflow/overflow.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft stack <input> [options]
.IP
\fBOptions:\fR
.RS
.TP
.B --trace
Show per-instruction execution trace with depth bars
.TP
.B --limit <n>
Max trace lines to display (default: 50)
.RE
.TP
.B test
Test round-trip bytecode → opcodes → bytecode fidelity.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft test <input>
.TP
.B decompile, dec
Decompile bytecode to Solidity-like pseudocode with automatic function inference, storage analysis, and pattern matching. Works on unverified contracts without an ABI. Output is syntax-highlighted and streamed character-by-character for an AI-like experience.
.IP
\fBUsage:\fR d_tuft decompile <input> [options]
.IP
\fBOptions:\fR
.RS
.TP
.B -o, --output <file>
Write decompiled output to file
.TP
.B --format <format>
Output format: solidity (default), pseudocode
.TP
.B --no-storage
Hide inferred storage variables
.TP
.B --no-comments
Hide decompiler comments and confidence scores
.TP
.B --no-stream
Print output instantly instead of streaming (useful for piping)
.TP
.B --rpc <url>
RPC endpoint to fetch bytecode from (default: public Ethereum RPC)
.RE
.IP
\fBExamples:\fR
.RS
.TP
Decompile from a local bytecode file:
d_tuft decompile contract.bin -o output.sol
.TP
Decompile a deployed contract by address:
d_tuft decompile 0x1234...abcd
.TP
Decompile from hex string:
d_tuft decompile 0x6080604052...
.TP
Decompile using a custom RPC endpoint:
d_tuft decompile 0x1234...abcd --rpc https://mainnet.infura.io/v3/YOUR_KEY
.RE
.SH INPUT FORMATS
All commands accepting bytecode support:
.IP \[bu] 2
Hex strings with 0x prefix (e.g., 0x6060...)
.IP \[bu] 2
Files containing hex bytecode
.IP \[bu] 2
Ethereum contract addresses (0x + 40 hex chars) for decompile command
.IP \[bu] 2
Assembly files (.evm) for the asm command
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable with optional PC, gas, hex annotations
.TP
.B annotated
Box-drawing table with gas costs and full details
.TP
.B json
Machine-readable JSON for programmatic processing
.TP
.B solidity
Decompiled Solidity-like code (decompile command only)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid input, mismatch, or failure)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Disassemble with full annotations:
d_tuft disasm contract.bin --format annotated --stack --gas
.TP
Compare two contract versions:
d_tuft diff v1.bin v2.bin --format annotated
.TP
Find gas hotspots:
d_tuft gas contract.bin --functions --top 10
.TP
Decompile an unverified contract:
d_tuft decompile 0x1f9840a85d5aF5bf1D1762F925BDADdC4201F984 -o uniswap.sol
.SH LIBRARY API
d_tuft can be imported as a TypeScript library:
.IP
.nf
import { core, evm, fi, decompiler } from 'd_tuft';

// Disassemble
const result = core.disassemble('0x6001600201');

// Execute
const vm = new evm.Evm('0x600160020100');
const execResult = vm.run();

// Identify functions
const fi = new fi.FunctionIdentifier(bytecode);
const functions = fi.identify();

// Decompile
const decompiled = decompiler.decompile(bytecode);
console.log(decompiled.solidity);
.fi
